From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WXbet <57314510+WXbet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:31:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/49] ffmpeg-ext: dashdec, a SegmentTemplate with a duration
 is not seekable

Ported to FFmpeg 9.0.2 from 0014-dashdec-segment-template-not-seekable.patch.
Port: applied clean (offset only). The patch file has no header; author
and subject are taken from the oe-alliance-core commit that added it.
---
 libavformat/dashdec.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/dashdec.c b/libavformat/dashdec.c
index e27c7e73..efbc300b 100644
--- a/libavformat/dashdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/dashdec.c
@@ -2168,7 +2168,9 @@ static int reopen_demux_for_component(AVFormatContext *s, struct representation
     ffio_init_context(&pls->pb, avio_ctx_buffer, INITIAL_BUFFER_SIZE, 0,
                       pls, read_data, NULL, c->is_live && !c->is_startover ? NULL : seek_data);
 
-    if(pls->type == AVMEDIA_TYPE_SUBTITLE || pls->n_timelines || pls->n_fragments > 1 || c->is_live)
+    /* a SegmentTemplate with a duration has neither timelines nor fragments,
+     * but many segments: only a single file is seekable */
+    if(pls->type == AVMEDIA_TYPE_SUBTITLE || pls->n_timelines || pls->n_fragments > 1 || pls->url_template || c->is_live)
     {
         pls->pb.pub.seekable = 0;
     }
